  "body": "Part of #904 (its point 4, and a note from PR #911's high-tier review).\n\nThe reduced-fidelity refusal says \"re-import with a larger budget\" (the maintainer's wording on #864), but the budget is the constant `MAX_FACETS` in `app` `geometry/import/step.rs`. The user cannot raise it.\n\n**What is owed.** A facet budget the user can set for a STEP import:\n\n- the import dialog (and the \"Update model\" path that re-imports),\n- the script verb,\n- MCP `import_model` (an optional `facet_budget` argument; `get_job` already reports the achieved approximation).\n\n`step::with_facet_budget` already scopes a budget for tests; the commands need to carry the number so undo/redo re-import the same mesh. A ceiling is still needed so a huge budget cannot exhaust memory: refuse past it by name.\n\n**Done means:** a STEP that imports at reduced fidelity under the default budget imports at full fidelity when the user raises the budget through the dialog, the script verb and MCP; the refusal text names a setting that exists; a budget past the ceiling is refused by name.\n",
